\chapter{Operational Envelope and Stability Regimes of the Temporal Symmetry Systems Engine (TSSE)}
\section{Overview}

Chapter 8 formalizes the operational envelope, stability regimes, and admissible
dynamical domains of the Temporal Symmetry Systems Engine (TSSE). Building upon the
axioms, Hamiltonian foundations, relativistic propulsion kernels, fusion energetic
kernels, structural invariant computation, and verification formalism established in
Chapters 1–7, this chapter defines the complete set of conditions under which TSSE
systems—including the integrated TSSE–AITFE engine—operate stably, predictably, and
within invariant-preserving manifolds.

The TSSE Operational Envelope and Stability Regimes (TSSE-OESR) define:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item The admissible dynamical domain of TSSE evolution.
  \item The stability regimes for temporal, relativistic, and fusion subsystems.
  \item The invariant-preserving operational envelope.
  \item The perturbation thresholds for TSSE stability.
  \item The canonical TSSE Stability Kernel (TSSE-SK).
\end{enumerate}

This chapter establishes the complete mathematical and structural blueprint for
TSSE operational stability.

