\section{Admissible Dynamical Domain}

Let $(q,p)$ denote the canonical coordinates of the TSSE-governed system. The
admissible dynamical domain is defined as:
\[
\mathcal{D}_{\text{TSSE}} =
\left\{
(q,p) \in \mathbb{R}^{2n}
\;\middle|\;
(q,p) \in \mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}},\;
H_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}(q,p) < \infty
\right\}.
\]

\begin{definition}[TSSE Admissible Domain]
The TSSE admissible domain $\mathcal{D}_{\text{TSSE}}$ is the set of all states
that lie within the composite structural manifold and possess finite Hamiltonian
energy.
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Domain Closure]
If $(q,p) \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{TSSE}}$, then:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)(q,p) \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{TSSE}}.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Since $\mathcal{U}(t)$ preserves manifold closure and Hamiltonian energy, the
domain remains invariant under evolution.
\end{proof}

This lemma establishes the admissible dynamical domain of TSSE systems.

