\section{Invariant-Preserving Operational Envelope}

Define the operational envelope:
\[
\mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}} =
\left\{
(q,p) \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{TSSE}}
\;\middle|\;
\mathcal{I}_{\text{TSSE}}(q,p) = \text{constant}
\right\}.
\]

\begin{definition}[TSSE Operational Envelope]
The TSSE operational envelope is the set of all states that preserve TSSE invariants
under evolution.
\end{definition}

\begin{theorem}[Operational Envelope Invariance]
If $(q,p) \in \mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}}$, then:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)(q,p) \in \mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}}.
\]
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Invariant preservation under symplectic evolution ensures that all states remain
within the operational envelope.
\end{proof}

This theorem establishes the invariant-preserving operational domain of TSSE engines.

