\section{Canonical TSSE Stability Kernel (TSSE-SK)}

Define the TSSE Stability Kernel:
\[
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-SK}} =
\left(
\mathcal{D}_{\text{TSSE}},\;
\mathcal{R}_{\text{TSSE}},\;
\mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}},\;
\epsilon_{\text{max}},\;
\mathcal{U}(t)
\right).
\]

It enforces:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{D}_{\text{TSSE}} = \mathcal{D}_{\text{TSSE}},
\qquad
\mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}} = \mathcal{E}_{\text{TSSE}},
\qquad
\epsilon < \epsilon_{\text{max}}.
\]

This kernel defines the complete operational stability architecture of TSSE engines.

